│ patch_description        │ The current spec uses 4 RY bands + 4 RZ bands + 2 CRZ params = 10 distinct params/block   │
│                          │ (62 total params), achieving perfect accuracy with score 0.90. Since train/val/test       │
│                          │ accuracy is already saturated at 1.00, there is clear room for further parameter economy. │
│                          │ I reduce the banding granularity from mod-4 to mod-2 (alternating even/odd qubits share   │
│                          │ the same RY and RZ angles), cutting single-qubit params per block from 8 to 4 (2 RY + 2   │
│                          │ RZ), while keeping the same ring CZ topology and the 2 shared CRZ parameters. This drops  │
│                          │ distinct params per block from 10 to 6, reducing total circuit params from 60 to 36 (plus │
│                          │ 2 readout = 38 total), a ~39% reduction. Given the task's strong reward for parameter     │
│                          │ economy and that the model was already overparameterized for this task (perfect accuracy  │
│                          │ with large margin), this should improve the combined score through higher parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency while very likely preserving the perfect accuracy, since entangling layers (CZ │
│                          │ ring + CRZ) still provide qubit-specific phase structure necessary for the classification │
│                          │ task, and mod-2 banding still breaks qubit symmetry enough given the alternating ring     │
│                          │ entanglers.                                                                               │
