│ patch_description        │ This candidate reduces trainable parameters back to the proven-efficient regime (3        │
│                          │ parameters per block × 6 repeats = 18 circuit params + 2 readout = 20 total), matching    │
│                          │ the best-observed configuration in prior experiments. It uses a single shared RY rotation │
│                          │ layer, a shared parametrized ZZ entangling chain (replacing fixed CZ gates with a         │
│                          │ trainable Ising ZZ interaction, allowing the entangling strength to be learned rather     │
│                          │ than fixed), and a single shared RZ rotation layer. This design maximizes parameter       │
│                          │ sharing (only 3 unique parameter names per block) while retaining full connectivity       │
│                          │ across the qubit chain, aiming to reproduce the perfect train/val/test accuracy and low   │
│                          │ loss seen in the best prior run, with maximal parameter economy and fast convergence.     │
