│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate combines the strongest elements from the prior programs. The 3-parameter   │
│                          │ fully-shared-per-block design (RY tilt on all qubits, ZZ ring entangler on all 8 edges,   │
│                          │ RZ phase on all qubits) achieved the best combined score with only 20 total parameters    │
│                          │ (18 circuit + 2 readout), full accuracy (train/val/test = 1.00), zero generalization gap, │
│                          │ and the best parameter_efficiency_mean (0.05) among all candidates. The other variants    │
│                          │ (10-param/block with 62 total params, and 5-param/block with 32 total params) added more  │
│                          │ parameters without any accuracy or convergence benefit — they simply spent more parameter │
│                          │ budget to reach the same perfect performance level, which is penalized by the             │
│                          │ parameter-economy objective.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crossover here keeps the winning ultra-compact ANSATZ_SPEC (3 shared params:          │
│                          │ ry_shared, zz_shared, rz_shared) as the core design, since it already saturates           │
│                          │ achievable accuracy while minimizing parameters. This maximizes the "parameter economy"   │
│                          │ reward while preserving full entangling connectivity (complete ring of ZZ gates spanning  │
│                          │ all 8 qubits) and collective single-qubit control (shared RY tilt + shared RZ phase),     │
│                          │ which was shown empirically sufficient for the classification task. All other fixed       │
│                          │ training/dataset/readout code is preserved unchanged as required.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Design justification for keeping the "tilt+twist+phase" pattern but not the               │
│                          │ symmetry-breaking or asymmetric-pair extensions: those additions (break_ry/break_rz on    │
│                          │ qubit 0, or zz_even/zz_odd splitting) increase the parameter count by 60-70% without any  │
│                          │ measurable accuracy or convergence gain in the given metrics table — so the additional    │
│                          │ capacity is unused/wasted budget under this metric.                                       │
