│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate (32 params: tilt, twist, phase, break_ry, break_rz) achieves the    │
│                          │ same perfect accuracy as the simpler 20-param version (tilt, twist, phase only) from a    │
│                          │ prior generation, but with lower parameter efficiency (0.03 vs 0.05) and higher           │
│                          │ depth/gate count. Since the scoring rewards parameter economy and the symmetry-breaking   │
│                          │ terms provide no measurable accuracy gain over the pure collective-spin model, we remove  │
│                          │ the `break_ry`/`break_rz` single-qubit correction terms on qubit 0. This reduces          │
│                          │ per-block distinct params from 5 to 3, cutting total circuit params from 30 to 18 (32     │
│                          │ total to 20 total), while preserving the full-strength collective tilt/twist/phase        │
│                          │ structure that already delivers 100% train/val/test accuracy. This directly optimizes the │
│                          │ parameter-economy objective without sacrificing convergence speed, since the removed      │
│                          │ terms were likely redundant with the permutation-symmetric readout (mean of Z-Z           │
│                          │ correlators is itself permutation-invariant, making per-qubit symmetry breaking less      │
│                          │ useful).                                                                                  │
